<title>SRI LANKA: Weather - Occasional showers seen over Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather - Occasional showers seen over Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Thursday morning</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Bowathenna		0</p>
<p>    Canyon		   41.8</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	    34.6</p>
<p>    Kotmale		  20.0</p>
<p>    Laxapana		 29.2</p>
<p>    Moussakele	     22.1</p>
<p>    Norton		   37.1</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    5.0</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   1.7</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
<p>The department said occasional showers accompanied by thunder at times will be experienced in the Western, Central, Sabaragamuwa and Southern provinces on Friday. Light showers may spread to the northcentral and Uva provinces.</p>
</text>
